 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? For a thick oil painting, two to three weeks in a warm, dry room is usually enough. If you varnished it today, it would still be wet tomorrow. Let it dry for at least two weeks first. Yes, a spray on protective coating you can reapply every few years. Most artists like the look of bare canvas better. It' feel slightly tacky to the touch, like it' still sticky. That's normal after the first few days.",
